r/appendix.tex\n-\\paragraph{Leaderboard groups by uploader.} Holding out the 717 uploaders instead of the 475 family stems (G split, same 50 splits, k grid and rank grid; the bootstrap resamples uploaders) gives a floor of 4.79 points (4.82 with families) and a gain of S6 over S0 of 2.11, 1.88, 1.35, 0.79, 0.44 and 0.25 points at $k=1$, 2, 3, 5, 8 and 13 (2.10, 1.84, 1.40, 0.77, 0.44, 0.28 with families), each inside the 90\\% interval of the family run. $k^*$ at $\\delta_{\\text{floor}}$ is 5 [3, 5] against 3 [3, 5], one grid step, and the excess at $k=3$ (1.12) sits at the margin (1.12). The training-side rule was not re-run on this grouping, and the strongest-quarter split is unchanged.\n+\\paragraph{Leaderboard groups by uploader.} Holding out the 717 uploaders instead of the 475 family stems (G split, same 50 splits, k grid and rank grid; the bootstrap resamples uploaders) gives a floor of 4.79 points (4.82 with families) and a gain of S6 over S0 (both with the factor-model posterior mean) of 2.11, 1.88, 1.35, 0.79, 0.44 and 0.25 points at $k=1$, 2, 3, 5, 8 and 13 (2.10, 1.84, 1.40, 0.77, 0.44, 0.28 with families), within 0.05 point of the family run at every $k$. $k^*$ at $\\delta_{\\text{floor}}$ is 5 [3, 5] against 3 [3, 5], one grid step, and the excess at $k=3$ (1.12) sits at the margin (1.12). The training-side rule was not re-run on this grouping, and the strongest-quarter split is unchanged.\n\nShell cwd was reset to /hutian/repo\n```", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "4645f79e-25a0-5bc0-a13d-61b4c64e1199", "at": 1795740349.5186667, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 84581, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.session/request_permission", "role": "idea-repo", "actor": "idea-repo", "execution_id": "228ba3ae74f9d52a12a7e1a1e082cad2", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "session/request_permission"}, {"id": "f8e93c38-aee5-5e5e-a8c2-3b538317189